.TH "HTMLTABLEELEMENT" "3JS" "August 19, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
HTMLTableElement \- HTMLTableElement
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]HTMLTableElement\f[B]\f[R] interface provides special
properties and methods (beyond the regular \f[CR]HTMLElement\f[R] object
interface it also has available to it by inheritance) for manipulating
the layout and presentation of tables in an HTML document.
.SH INSTANCE PROPERTIES
\f[I]Inherits properties from its parent, \f[CI]HTMLElement\f[I].\f[R]
.TP
\f[B]HTMLTableElement.caption\f[R]
An \f[CR]HTMLTableCaptionElement\f[R] representing the first
\f[CR]<caption>\f[R] element child of the given \f[CR]<table>\f[R], or
\f[CR]null\f[R] if no such element exists.
This property can be assigned, which causes the existing first
\f[CR]<caption>\f[R] element child, if any, to be removed, and the given
value, if it is not \f[CR]null\f[R], to be inserted as the first child.
If the assigned value is not an \f[CR]HTMLTableCaptionElement\f[R] or
\f[CR]null\f[R], a \f[CR]TypeError\f[R] is thrown.
.TP
\f[B]HTMLTableElement.tHead\f[R]
An \f[CR]HTMLTableSectionElement\f[R] representing the first
\f[CR]<thead>\f[R] element child of the given \f[CR]<table>\f[R], or
\f[CR]null\f[R] if no such element exists.
This property can be assigned, which causes the existing first
\f[CR]<thead>\f[R] element child, if any, to be removed, and the given
value, if it is not \f[CR]null\f[R], to be inserted immediately before
the first element child that\(cqs neither a \f[CR]<caption>\f[R] nor a
\f[CR]<colgroup>\f[R], or as the last child if there is no such element.
If the assigned value is not an \f[CR]HTMLTableSectionElement\f[R] or
\f[CR]null\f[R], a \f[CR]TypeError\f[R] is thrown; otherwise, if it is
not a \f[CR]<thead>\f[R] element or \f[CR]null\f[R], a
\f[CR]HierarchyRequestError\f[R] \f[CR]DOMException\f[R] is thrown.
.TP
\f[B]HTMLTableElement.tFoot\f[R]
An \f[CR]HTMLTableSectionElement\f[R] representing the first
\f[CR]<tfoot>\f[R] element child of the given \f[CR]<table>\f[R], or
\f[CR]null\f[R] if no such element exists.
This property can be assigned, which causes the existing first
\f[CR]<tfoot>\f[R] element child, if any, to be removed, and the given
value, if it is not \f[CR]null\f[R], to be inserted as the last child.
If the assigned value is not an \f[CR]HTMLTableSectionElement\f[R] or
\f[CR]null\f[R], a \f[CR]TypeError\f[R] is thrown; otherwise, if it is
not a \f[CR]<tfoot>\f[R] element or \f[CR]null\f[R], a
\f[CR]HierarchyRequestError\f[R] \f[CR]DOMException\f[R] is thrown.
.TP
\f[B]HTMLTableElement.rows\f[R] \f[I](read\-only)\f[R]
Returns a live \f[CR]HTMLCollection\f[R] of all \f[CR]<tr>\f[R] elements
that are a child of the given \f[CR]<table>\f[R] element, or a child of
one of the table\(cqs \f[CR]<thead>\f[R], \f[CR]<tbody>\f[R], and
\f[CR]<tfoot>\f[R] children.
The members of the \f[CR]<thead>\f[R] appear first, followed by members
of the \f[CR]<tbody>\f[R] and the table itself, and members of the
\f[CR]<tfoot>\f[R] come last, sorted by tree order within each group.
The returned object is automatically updated when the
\f[CR]HTMLTableElement\f[R] changes.
.TP
\f[B]HTMLTableElement.tBodies\f[R] \f[I](read\-only)\f[R]
Returns a live \f[CR]HTMLCollection\f[R] of all \f[CR]<tbody>\f[R]
element children of the given \f[CR]<table>\f[R].
The returned object is automatically updated when the
\f[CR]HTMLTableElement\f[R] changes.
.SS Obsolete Properties
.RS
.PP
\f[B]Warning:\f[R] The following properties are obsolete.
You should avoid using them.
.RE
.TP
\f[B]HTMLTableElement.align\f[R] \f[I](deprecated)\f[R]
A string containing an enumerated value reflecting the \f[CR]align\f[R]
attribute.
It indicates the alignment of the element\(cqs contents with respect to
the surrounding context.
The possible values are \f[CR]\(dqleft\(dq\f[R],
\f[CR]\(dqright\(dq\f[R], and \f[CR]\(dqcenter\(dq\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]HTMLTableElement.bgColor\f[R] \f[I](deprecated)\f[R]
A string containing the background color of the cells.
It reflects the obsolete \f[CR]bgColor\f[R] attribute.
.TP
\f[B]HTMLTableElement.border\f[R] \f[I](deprecated)\f[R]
A string containing the width in pixels of the border of the table.
It reflects the obsolete \f[CR]border\f[R] attribute.
.TP
\f[B]HTMLTableElement.cellPadding\f[R] \f[I](deprecated)\f[R]
A string containing the width in pixels of the horizontal and vertical
space between cell content and cell borders.
It reflects the obsolete \f[CR]cellpadding\f[R] attribute.
.TP
\f[B]HTMLTableElement.cellSpacing\f[R] \f[I](deprecated)\f[R]
A string containing the width in pixels of the horizontal and vertical
separation between cells.
It reflects the obsolete \f[CR]cellspacing\f[R] attribute.
.TP
\f[B]HTMLTableElement.frame\f[R] \f[I](deprecated)\f[R]
A string containing the type of the external borders of the table.
It reflects the obsolete \f[CR]frame\f[R] attribute and can take one of
the following values: \f[CR]\(dqvoid\(dq\f[R], \f[CR]\(dqabove\(dq\f[R],
\f[CR]\(dqbelow\(dq\f[R], \f[CR]\(dqhsides\(dq\f[R],
\f[CR]\(dqvsides\(dq\f[R], \f[CR]\(dqlhs\(dq\f[R],
\f[CR]\(dqrhs\(dq\f[R], \f[CR]\(dqbox\(dq\f[R], or
\f[CR]\(dqborder\(dq\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]HTMLTableElement.rules\f[R] \f[I](deprecated)\f[R]
A string containing the type of the internal borders of the table.
It reflects the obsolete \f[CR]rules\f[R] attribute and can take one of
the following values: \f[CR]\(dqnone\(dq\f[R],
\f[CR]\(dqgroups\(dq\f[R], \f[CR]\(dqrows\(dq\f[R],
\f[CR]\(dqcols\(dq\f[R], or \f[CR]\(dqall\(dq\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]HTMLTableElement.summary\f[R] \f[I](deprecated)\f[R]
A string containing a description of the purpose or the structure of the
table.
It reflects the obsolete \f[CR]summary\f[R] attribute.
.TP
\f[B]HTMLTableElement.width\f[R] \f[I](deprecated)\f[R]
A string containing the length in pixels or in percentage of the desired
width of the entire table.
It reflects the obsolete \f[CR]width\f[R] attribute.
.SH INSTANCE METHODS
\f[I]Inherits methods from its parent, \f[CI]HTMLElement\f[I]\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]HTMLTableElement.createTHead()\f[R]
Creates a \f[CR]<thead>\f[R] element, inserts it before the first
element child of the given \f[CR]<table>\f[R] that\(cqs neither a
\f[CR]<caption>\f[R] nor a \f[CR]<colgroup>\f[R], or as the last child
if no such insertion location is found, and returns it.
If the table already has a \f[CR]<thead>\f[R] element child, this method
returns the first such child without creating one.
.TP
\f[B]HTMLTableElement.deleteTHead()\f[R]
Removes the first \f[CR]<thead>\f[R] element child from a given
\f[CR]<table>\f[R], if any.
.TP
\f[B]HTMLTableElement.createTFoot()\f[R]
Creates a \f[CR]<tfoot>\f[R] element, inserts it as the last child of
the given \f[CR]<table>\f[R], and returns it.
If the table already has a \f[CR]<tfoot>\f[R] element child, this method
returns the first such child without creating one.
.TP
\f[B]HTMLTableElement.deleteTFoot()\f[R]
Removes the first \f[CR]<tfoot>\f[R] element child from a given
\f[CR]<table>\f[R], if any.
.TP
\f[B]HTMLTableElement.createTBody()\f[R]
Creates a \f[CR]<tbody>\f[R] element, inserts it immediately after the
last \f[CR]<tbody>\f[R] element child of the given \f[CR]<table>\f[R],
or as the last child if there is no such element, and returns it.
.TP
\f[B]HTMLTableElement.createCaption()\f[R]
Creates a \f[CR]<caption>\f[R] element, inserts it as the first child of
the given \f[CR]<table>\f[R], and returns it.
If the table already has a \f[CR]<caption>\f[R] element child, this
method returns the first such child without creating one.
.TP
\f[B]HTMLTableElement.deleteCaption()\f[R]
Removes the first \f[CR]<caption>\f[R] element child from a given
\f[CR]<table>\f[R], if any.
.TP
\f[B]HTMLTableElement.insertRow()\f[R]
Creates a \f[CR]<tr>\f[R] element, inserts it at the specified position
in the \f[CR]rows\f[R] collection, and returns it.
If the \f[CR]rows\f[R] collection is empty and the table also has no
\f[CR]<tbody>\f[R] elements, a \f[CR]<tbody>\f[R] element is first
created and inserted.
.TP
\f[B]HTMLTableElement.deleteRow()\f[R]
Removes a specific row (\f[CR]<tr>\f[R]) from a given
\f[CR]<table>\f[R].
If \f[CR]index\f[R] is \f[CR]\-1\f[R], the last row is removed.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Using the DOM Table Interface
The \f[CR]HTMLTableElement\f[R] interface provides some convenience
methods for creating and manipulating tables.
Two frequently used methods are \f[CR]HTMLTableElement.insertRow\f[R]
and \f[CR]HTMLTableRowElement.insertCell\f[R].
.PP
To add a row and some cells to an existing table:
.IP
.EX
<\f[B]table\f[R] id=\(dqtable0\(dq>
  <\f[B]tbody\f[R]>
    <\f[B]tr\f[R]>
      <\f[B]td\f[R]>Row 0 Cell 0</\f[B]td\f[R]>
      <\f[B]td\f[R]>Row 0 Cell 1</\f[B]td\f[R]>
    </\f[B]tr\f[R]>
  </\f[B]tbody\f[R]>
</\f[B]table\f[R]>
.EE
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] table = document.getElementById(\(dqtable0\(dq);
\f[B]const\f[R] row = table.insertRow(\-1);

\f[B]for\f[R] (\f[B]let\f[R] i = 0; i < 2; i++) {
  \f[B]const\f[R] cell = row.insertCell(\-1);
  \f[B]const\f[R] text = \(gaRow ${row.rowIndex} Cell ${i}\(ga;
  cell.appendChild(document.createTextNode(text));
}
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.IP \(bu 2
The HTML element implementing this interface: \f[CR]<table>\f[R].
